MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_001: *sigh*
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_002: <NCA>"You're alone. That's rare."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_003: Promised One. As it happens, I was in a beauty's\nbedroom only moments ago.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_004: I hope you'll permit my talking to myself...
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_005: Even on the nights I share with others, I sometimes\nfeel overcome with the most desperate loneliness.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_006: I know not what my parents look like. Yes, Kalla has\nalways been something like a mother...
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_007: But there's a hole in my heart that remains unfilled.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_008: On nights like that, when that emptiness feels too\nmuch to bear, I go outside and gaze at the sky.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_009: Seeing me in this state, what must you think?
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_010: <NCA>"I thought you were talking to yourself."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_011: The wind's a fickle thing, and blows where it will.\nI just thought I'd ask.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_012: I've always felt a certain kinship with you.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_013: Sirocco, who goes with the breeze, and the Herald\nwho swept into Dagda.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_014: There's something to that, isn't there? Though you\nhave an otherworldliness that sets you apart.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_015: A quality that's...not entirely human. Perhaps that's\nthe reason I'm spilling my guts.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_016: Do you have a family, Promised One? Parents?
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_017: <NCA>"I'm not sure how to answer that."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_018: <NCB>"Not anymore, I don't think."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_019: <ACA>Hehe. Mysteries upon mysteries. That's fine,\nI won't pry.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_020: <ACB>I see. Well, I won't pry.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_021: Normally, because of the nature of my work, I'd\nlook into it. But I just want to enjoy this night.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_A_022: To gaze at the sky with you until morning.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_001: ♪
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_002: Rather late, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_003: Where was it you wandered off to? The nights are\nmuch less enjoyable without you.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_004: <NCA>"Sorry about that."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_005: Don't apologize. Really, I'm just glad you're back.\nI was almost numb with cold when you were gone...
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_006: There were times I stopped believing you'd\never return.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_007: It's funny, isn't it? A man who usually burns with\npassion, in a land on fire—and I felt chilled with fear.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_008: <NCA>"There's nothing funny about it."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_009: <NCB>"You won't be cold anymore."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_010: <ACA>Ha... You always know how to set me off balance.\nI'm not sure what to say.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_011: <ACB>No, I won't. Not with you there to warm me.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_012: Why do I get the sense you're not planning to\nstick around? You intend to go elsewhere.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_013: You're like me—a breeze. A migratory bird.\nYou can't stay in one place.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_014: <NCA>"There are people who still need saving."
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_015: Yes, I suppose so. Gods! You tease.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_016: You can't leave me in the cold again—please!
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_017: Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_018: Would you look at that? I'm starting to sound like the\nbeauties I talk to.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_019: You have a way of making me lower my defenses,\nPromised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_020: Fine. I won't stop you. But. But!
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_021: <RSDS>If you're going, then I'm coming with you.\nWe'll blow across the world like a fiery wind.
MID_SE_Ism_Sci_S_022: Coolly I sweep forth, but with a raging passion. I am\nSyracusio of the Silver Hail!